## Bug Reports

- [x] (UI) WebUI settings save -> Internal Server Error
- [ ] KeyboardInterrupt handling in daemon.py: Ctrl+C may crash the program instead of
      shutting down gracefully. The try/except around the main loop should catch
      KeyboardInterrupt but may not work properly due to how asyncio.run() handles
      exceptions during initialization vs. execution.
- [d] settings.toml race condition: `Configurable.save_config()`,
      `Configurable._cleanup_legacy_keys()`, and `write_registry_entry()` (base.py) all
      read the whole settings.toml, modify one part, and write the whole file back,
      without any lock. Two of these running interleaved on the event loop (e.g. one
      module's settings save racing another module being added via the web UI) can
      lose whichever write finishes its read first. Fix would be a shared asyncio.Lock
      around all three read-modify-write paths.


